{
  "category": "strip_and_expose",
  "version": "1.0",
  "description": "Strip and expose (issue #543, RFC U6): esm_problem's `strip` removes the named construct classes from what the build lowers and hands them back as one object (`stripped`), and `compile_kernels` compiles observeds and expressions as kernels sharing the stripped right-hand side's ABI, k(out, u, z, p, t, dt). Generated by scripts/gen-strip-and-expose-manifest.py; every kernel anchor is analytic.",
  "spec": [
    "API_SPEC.md §5.8 (Strip and expose)",
    "CONFORMANCE_SPEC.md §5.57",
    "esm-libraries-spec.md §2.5.13"
  ],
  "bindings": {
    "julia": "every section",
    "rust": "every section",
    "python": "per_class, stripped_goldens, not_solvable, and compile_kernels refused with compiler_unavailable"
  },
  "classes": [
    "continuous_events",
    "discrete_events",
    "parameter_updates",
    "algebraic"
  ],
  "tolerance_classes": {
    "algebraic": {
      "rtol": 1e-13,
      "atol": 1e-300
    },
    "note": "CONFORMANCE_SPEC §5.38.2; |got - want| <= atol + rtol |want|"
  },
  "probe_inputs": "u and z name every block of state_layout(ks) / z_layout(ks) by flattened name (a number for a 0-d block, a column-major list for an array block); p is parameter_vector(ks, {}) (the declared defaults); forcing is default_forcing_set(ks). `u: null` in remaining_rhs means the program's default state (each state's starting value). expected maps a kernel_layout label to its values; `u` is the whole output of a map kernel and `du` that of the rhs kernel.",
  "default_refusal": {
    "manifest": "../unsupported_construct/manifest.json",
    "note": "With strip empty every refusal case of CONFORMANCE_SPEC §5.39 still refuses; that category's own adapters gate it."
  },
